    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW24q3T9CwWwRn94Pkb1THGGV)_\n\n## Summary\nFollows #221 (merged). Changes what `sp-litnotes-titles` writes:\n\n- **Title:** last names only, from `pub-author`, `pub-year` and `pub-title`: `Reuten (2014) The value form as a social form`. Two authors `A and B`, three `A, B and C`, four or more the first two and `et al.` (`A, B et al.`; `sp-litnotes-titles-et-al-from`). `pub-author` is read as `Last, First`, `First Last` (lower-case particles stay with the surname), `[[id:..][Name]]` links and quoted names, split at `;`, `and` or between links.\n- **Failures:** a missing `pub-year` fails (no `n.d.`), as do a missing or empty `pub-title`, a missing `pub-author` and an ambiguous one (a piece with several commas). The report lists them under `Failed: ...` with what the note has, and counts them.\n- **Asking:** `sp-litnotes-titles-apply` offers to fill in the failed items: one question per missing value (title, authors as `Last, First; Last, First`, year), an empty answer skips. The answers are used for the title only; the note's meta lines are not changed. The report is shown again, then the single write confirmation.\n- **File name:** the first citation key alone (`ROAM_REFS`, or `#+reference:` for notes #210's conversion has not reached), `reuten2014value.org`. Not renamed and listed: no key, a key whose file exists, a key two notes share, case-only differences.\n- Still: report first, time-stamped backups, `:ID:` checked, Vulpea db updated, `file:` links to old names listed.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 8 ERT tests (`tests/sp-litnotes-titles-test.el`) in Emacs 29.3 batch: authors, formatting, keys, statuses, report writes nothing, apply is idempotent, unsaved buffer skipped, apply asks for missing values (prompts stubbed). Tangle check passes.\n- [ ] Run `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-report` on the real litnotes and read the title column and the `Failed:` groups before `sp-litnotes-titles-apply`.\n- [ ] Not run: the real Vulpea database calls, the real vault.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBPPHfzgLTkNeDC4q4",
